 "result": "VACASK keeps case: op2.raw has A and a, and rawfile.read(...).index('A'): \"'A' matches several variables: A, a\"; save default (bytewise sorted) writes d1:a_int, d1:implicit_equation_0, e1:flow(br), I2:vx:flow(br), IPRB:flow(br) (+4.8125e-07 into in); save full adds d1:implicit_equation_1, d1:qp_int, d1:sw_int; save default p(r1, i) gives the defaults plus r1.i = 5e-4 A into terminal 1 (measured 5.1875e-4 in this divider); noise n() in engine order, nc(r1) nc('I2:r3') exactly those with their contributions, a diode's rs id flicker rsw idsw flickersw; acxf writes tf()/zin() of IPRB, v1 and I2:vx, and tf(i1) = 500 for 1 kOhm||1 kOhm; strictsave=0: a nosuch column of zeros, rc 0; 1 and 2: \"Node 'nosuch' not found. Failed to bind analysis outputs.\", no rawfile; under 2 an nc() before an op is still ignored. Xyce: V(*) names V(XI2:MID) and no device internal; DNO(XI2:R3); I(R1) 0.0005187502 A into terminal 1, I(E1) -0.0009625; .print dc ... v(I2:MID): \"There was 1 undefined symbol in .PRINT command: node I2:MID\", rc 1; .ic v(I2:MID)=0.3: \"Ignoring nodes: I2:MID\", rc 0, V(XI2:MID) = 1.0 at t = 0",
 "rules": [
  "\u00a76.1 what is saved: save default on VACASK writes bytewise-sorted node and flow columns plus device internals, which vamos ignores; save full adds more",
  "\u00a76.3/\u00a76.4 the forward name map: I2:Mid / V(XI2:MID), r1.i / I(R1) (positive into terminal 1), e1:flow(br) / I(E1), DNO(XI2:R3); nodes A and a are distinct columns on VACASK, so Raw.exact is used (index('A') is ambiguous)",
  "\u00a77.1 noise: nc(inst) gives exactly n(inst) and its contributions; acxf writes tf()/zin() of every source; \u00a78.4 a diode's contributions rs id flicker rsw idsw flickersw",
  "\u00a77.1 strictsave: vamos sets strictsave=2 so an unknown save fails the analysis (no rawfile) instead of a column of zeros",
  "\u00a74.5 item 15 printed_path: Xyce needs the X-prefixed spelling in .PRINT and .IC"
